# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  'SNYK-JS-INFLIGHT-6095116':
    - '*':
        reason: 'Transitively pulled in by ExcelJS, via archiver > archiver-utils > glob and via unzipper > fstream > rimraf > glob, and by eslint > file-entry-cache > flat-cache > rimraf > glob. Test-only tooling that runs briefly and exits on controlled, local/test inputs; memory-leak impact is not exploitable in this context and there is no upstream fix.'
        expires: '2028-01-01T00:00:00.000Z'
  # Zip Slip in unzipper. Triggers only when extracting archive entries to disk.
  # unzipper reaches us via exceljs, used by the test data/spreadsheet
  # generators, which read xlsx zips in memory (unzipper.Open.buffer) and never
  # extract entries to the filesystem. The advisory has no upstream patch: it was
  # verified in this run that even the latest unzipper (0.12.5) is still flagged,
  # and overriding to it also breaks exceljs (which pins 0.10.x).
  'SNYK-JS-UNZIPPER-18365659':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Disk-extraction-only Zip Slip sink in unzipper, reached only through
          exceljs in the test data generators, which parse xlsx in memory and
          never extract to disk. No upstream patch (latest unzipper 0.12.5 is
          still flagged and is incompatible with exceljs). Test-only tooling.
        expires: 2027-03-21T00:00:00.000Z
  # ReDoS in basic-ftp's Client.list() directory-listing parser. basic-ftp
  # reaches us only via browserstack-node-sdk > pac-proxy-agent > get-uri, and
  # only when a PAC file is fetched from an ftp:// URL. The suite configures its
  # outbound proxy as a plain HTTP_PROXY (undici ProxyAgent), never a PAC file.
  # The fix (6.2.1) is a major bump; every get-uri release pins basic-ftp ^5.
  'SNYK-JS-BASICFTP-20419408':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          ReDoS in basic-ftp Client.list(), reached only when pac-proxy-agent
          fetches a PAC file over ftp://. The suite uses a plain HTTP_PROXY, no
          PAC file. Fix is basic-ftp 6.x but get-uri pins ^5 in every release.
          Test-only BrowserStack tooling, not a production path.
        expires: 2027-04-26T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JS-MINIMATCH-22111072':
    - 'exceljs > *':
        reason: >-
          Pattern amplification in minimatch 3.x under glob 7, reached only
          through exceljs (archiver-utils and unzipper > fstream > rimraf).
          The fix is minimatch 11, which glob 7 cannot use, and exceljs has no
          release off glob 7. The globs are never fed attacker-controlled
          patterns. Test-only spreadsheet generators, not a production path.
        expires: 2027-02-16T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JS-BASICFTP-22549670':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Prototype pollution via a __proto__ fact name in a basic-ftp server
          response, reached only when pac-proxy-agent fetches a PAC file over
          ftp://. The suite uses a plain HTTP_PROXY, no PAC file. Fix is
          basic-ftp 6.x but get-uri (8.0.1, latest) still pins ^5.
          Test-only BrowserStack tooling, not a production path.
        expires: 2027-02-16T00:00:00.000Z
  'SNYK-JS-BASICFTP-22549672':
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Crash on CR/LF in an FTP password, reached only when pac-proxy-agent
          fetches a PAC file over ftp://. The suite uses a plain HTTP_PROXY, no
          PAC file, and passes no FTP credentials. Fix is basic-ftp 6.x but
          get-uri (8.0.1, latest) still pins ^5. Test-only BrowserStack
          tooling, not a production path.
        expires: 2027-02-16T00:00:00.000Z
